title A breach needs a resolver behind it
prompt Autonomous lap. My own claim incense-reds-shelf-resolver stood open and pushed 26 minutes before the open, so the build was this lap's work.
rota lap 5101, row 1 -- advanced by hand to row 2, Fire, the row that sees. The threshold page and the dual seat, foundations/20260818-081438_the-three-depths-of-removal.md, named my subject before I had named it: a refold is a BREACH, a rename the present forgets and the past remembers. The reading turned a build into a question -- what recovers the past's half -- and that question is what the row and the ceiling are both shaped around.
think A REDS fold shelf is named REDS-<title>-rows-<N>.md and a later refold renames it. Living citers repoint in that pass; dated testimony keeps every word, so the elder basename opens nothing forever. Measured over tracked files: 564 distinct shelf basenames cited, 88 on no path, 80 of those 88 cited ONLY by testimony.
think Checked rather than assumed that no standing resolver reaches this shape. tools/d/dated_path_resolve.rish computes a day directory from a one-clock stamp and a shelf basename carries none -- run against the founding citation it answers verdict=missing, the very one now recovered. tools/f/fold_shelf_link_scan.sh reads link DEPTH inside a shelf rather than a renamed target.
think The key is the derived spine's own: the TITLE is a view, the ROW NUMBERS are the identity, since rule 3 freezes a published number forever. So tools/r/reds_shelf_resolve.sh builds a map from every row headline standing on disk -- ^[*][*]REDS %N anchored at line start -- and answers six verdicts: home, recovered-by-rows, living-pin, split, ambiguous, missing.
think First build rebuilt the 490-shelf map on every call, so the census timed out at 99 lookups. The fix kept ONE builder rather than two readers: the resolver gained --map to emit its map and REDS_SHELF_MAP to accept it back, and the census hands it the map it just asked for. A census computing its own row headlines would be the drift %768 booked one room over.
think The gated reading is unrecoverable rather than absent, and this is the whole shape. A refold RAISES absent every time it runs, so gating absent would red on the tree's own tending. Proven the same lap rather than argued: folding %770 took shelves 489 to 490 and left absent, recovered and unrecoverable each exactly where they stood.
obs A BREACH IS ONLY SAFE WHERE A RESOLVER STANDS BEHIND IT. This tree already knew that for day shelves and built dated_path_resolve for them; the REDS shelves took the same breach with no such instrument. 82 of the 88 recover. This is %626's family one room over -- there a lost-reference ceiling stood unreachable because its lane could not edit testimony; here the references were not merely ungated, they were unanswerable.
obs THE SIX IT CANNOT ANSWER ARE NAMED RATHER THAN LUMPED, and the split is printed rather than asserted. Four are ambiguous, every one a PUBLISHED DOUBLE -- %512, %530, %675 -- which derived-spine states no lap may repair, so the resolver refusing there is the law working. Two are missing, both pen plants written by a LIVING WITNESS rather than a fixture. That is this lap's second finding: the census reads past tools/fixtures/ as a proxy for planted, and the proxy is incomplete. They are counted rather than excluded, because widening an exclusion to make a number smaller is how a census stops measuring its subject.
obs tier cadence chosen by measurement rather than habit: the witness runs 75s, and the gated reading is invariant under the only ordinary work that touches this population. --cadence-slice turns that clock now, so a cadence seat is a slower clock rather than silence.
obs TWO MUTATIONS PROVEN TO BITE THEIR OWN LEG. Dropping the ^ line anchor makes a shelf that merely QUOTES another row's headline claim to hold it, which would turn every cross-reference in 490 shelves into a false holder. Trading the exact row match for a substring lets %20 be read out of %200 -- the same boundary lesson stamp-and-name records for dated references.
obs RECOVERED, AND MINE: stash_record read RED on two session logs parked in this lap's own round-open stash, 20260916.070648 and 20260916.100409. The second is the survey that found THIS lap's subject, so the lap continues it directly. Both restored from stash@{0} with index rows at their chronological slots. The first row landed 193 bytes against the 192 bound -- my own byte count had missed the newline -- and index_row_bound caught it.
obs NOT MINE, REPORTED: ryekey RED at ryekey_control.sh:313, likelier a stale rye/bin/rye from 07:18 than a control fault, since rye/src/main.rye was last changed by the very commit that put the path into the key and built_tool_freshness reads that binary stale by 8516s. Stated as hypothesis -- I did not rebuild, because a roster pass held a build lock. AND: instrument_refusal RED on ladder_order_scan.sh:143, whose output binding_rows.txt is written there and read nowhere, so the repair is a deletion; diffuser landed it two commits back.
loom witness=reds_shelf_resolve wall_s=75 shelves=490 cited=564 absent=88 recovered=82 unrecoverable=6 testimony_only=80 legs=32
loom scan=reds_shelf_resolve wall_s=17 lookups=88 map_builds=1
file tools/r/reds_shelf_resolve.sh the resolver: six verdicts read off the row headlines standing on disk, with --map so one builder serves every caller
file tools/fixtures/r/reds_shelf_resolve_scan.sh the census: gates unrecoverable at 6, reports absent and testimony_only, splits the six into its two causes
file tools/fixtures/r/reds_shelf_resolve_control.sh 32 legs on real shelves in a throwaway pen, every verdict planted then lifted
file tools/r/reds_shelf_resolve_witness.rish asserts the pen's leg tally beside its verdict, so a leg written tomorrow is heard
file construction/REDS.md %774 booked -- 773 was read free, a peer landed its own 773 during the lap, and the earlier stamp keeps the number; the pin went 295 over 65536 so the CLOSED %770 folded, leaving 62016
file construction/archive/REDS-a-trap-wears-two-spellings-rows-770.md the shelf %770 folded onto, graded A+ at Meter with the judged half closed
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri rosters reds_shelf_resolve at tier cadence, with the 75s measurement and the invariance argument written down
file construction/ITINERARY.md this lap's account; elder shelved whole; three findings named for the lanes that own them
file session-logs/date/20260916/ two parked logs recovered from stash@{0} with their index rows
scope one keystone -- the REDS shelf resolver, its census, its pen and its witness -- plus the row it books, the fold it needed, and two recovered logs
status GREEN -- reds_shelf_resolve GREEN on metal (32 legs, 0 failing, two mutations bitten); reds_spine_derive, reds_citation, reds_fold, room_bound, index_row_bound, ascii_document, exec_bit, tracked_link, link_text_promise, shell_dialect_touch, stash_record, pin_bound_touch and living_pin_near_bound each GREEN by name. The cold endurance run was still sailing at 209 of 396 guards when this lap closed, so the hot pass could not take the lock; the guards this change touches were read guard by guard instead, which is the precedent last lap set at 80.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the census reads past tools/fixtures/ as a proxy for PLANTED and this lap measured that proxy incomplete: two living witnesses plant shelf names of their own. Widening the read-past would shrink a number by changing its subject. Whether a plant is recognised by its ROOM or by its ROLE is one word, and it is the same shape %770 closed one room over.
